 \subsection{Simulation Protocol}\label{sec:protocol}
 
 Each simulated day executes a fixed cycle (Fig.~\ref{fig:sim_loop}).
-Today's arrival is added to the residual from yesterday and the level is capped
-at bin capacity $E_i$. Overflow and lost mass are scored on that
-post-arrival, pre-collection state. The selection strategy then reads the true
-level and flags mandatory bins; the constructor builds a tour and the improver
-refines it; the tour is executed and the collected waste recorded; the day is
-logged and the residual level carried forward.
-The formulation uses the same fill-before-collection order, but retains
-excess mass. In the simulator, the decision level is
-$\min\{E_i,w_i^t+a_i^t\}$ and lost mass is
-$\ell_i^t=\max\{0,w_i^t+a_i^t-E_i\}$. After collection,
-$w_i^{t+1}=w_i^t+a_i^t-\ell_i^t-q_i^t$. Thus $w_i^t$ denotes
-the opening residual, not the post-arrival decision level.
+The model opens day $d$ at the state $w_{i,d}$, collects, and only then
+receives the deposits $a_{i,d}$ (Definition~\ref{def:mp-state}). The next
+opening state keeps every kilogram,
+$w_{i,d+1}=w_{i,d}-q_{i,d}+a_{i,d}$, including waste beside a full bin.
+The simulator applies that day's draw before the route. It adds the draw
+to the opening residual, caps the level at $\mathit{Cap}_i$, scores
+overflow and lost mass, and only then selects, builds, and executes the
+tour. When the opening residual is $w_{i,d}$, the level the policy sees is
+$\min\{\mathit{Cap}_i,\,w_{i,d}+a_{i,d}\}$, the lost mass is
+$\ell_{i,d}=\max\{0,\,w_{i,d}+a_{i,d}-\mathit{Cap}_i\}$, and the next
+opening residual is that capped level minus the kilograms collected.
+The orders agree only when nothing is discarded and the deposit is timed
+after collection. The reported indicator $o_{i,d}$ is one when the capped
+pre-collection level equals $\mathit{Cap}_i$. It is not the model's test
+$w_{i,d}>\mathit{Cap}_i$, which reads the opening state and counts an
+overflow inherited from the day before.
 A shift-length check sits between improvement and execution and does not
 apply to the VRPP setting used in these runs.
 The day's time is mandatory selection plus route construction plus route
