+\subsection{Data Integrity}\label{sec:integrity}
+
+The excluded runs are three at 30 days and one at 90 days, all SWC-TCF
+on Figueira da Foz under Gamma-3. They collect 30\% to 86\%
+less than their scenario median (Table~\ref{tab:excluded}). The constructors
+in a scenario share an arrival sequence, so the tonnage gap is a difference
+in what was collected from that sequence, not a difference in what arrived.
+The three 30-day logs contain a record for every day from 1 to 30.
+Look-ahead with either improver last collected on day 16, and Service-Level 2
+with Fast-TSP last collected on day 22; later days stay in the log with zero
+kilograms. The overflow count keeps rising on those days, because it counts
+every bin-day at capacity: the look-ahead logs end at 284 and 287 overflows
+on day 30 (2{,}168 and 2{,}166 over the month), and the Service-Level 2 log
+ends at 205 (757 over the month). The 90-day summary records 23{,}886
+overflows and 13 collection days. Its raw daily log is pending recovery, so
+those two numbers are not read as a day on which the run stopped.
+The cell is the largest network under the heavier generating process. The
+exclusion records the anomalous tonnage. It does not by itself identify a
+solver crash or a log that was cut short.
+
+The detection rule was a tonnage shortfall against the scenario median. 
+Outside these four runs the shortfall distribution has median $0.00$ and does not exceed $0.071$; the four sit at $0.30$, $0.47$, $0.47$ and $0.86$. 
+The gap identifies them unambiguously. Collection-day count cannot diagnose them: several strong policies collect on only 15 of 30 days because they bundle collections well. Tonnage provides the relevant signal.
+
+Excluding these runs alone would have introduced a subtler bias of the same
+family as the 90-day sampling problem: since all four are SWC-TCF's, removing
+only them would average SWC-TCF over the scenarios where it did not fail while
+averaging its rivals over those scenarios too. We therefore dropped the affected scenario cells for \emph{all} constructors, at a cost of 21 further dropped runs for the Figueira da Foz region, leaving 456 runs at 30 days with every constructor contributing exactly 57.
+
+
